      family: "accounting",
      requires: ["a share-pricing vault reachable by an unprivileged depositor", "totalAssets derived from a live balance read rather than an internal counter", "an empty or very small totalSupply at the target block", "a subsequent depositor (or a front-runnable one) to absorb the loss"],
      questions: ["Is totalAssets() computed from a live balanceOf(address(this)) donation-sensitive read, or from an internal counter only deposit and withdraw move?", "Is the vault totalSupply zero or economically tiny at the block where the attacker can first deposit?", "Is there a virtual-share offset, dead-share burn, or MINIMUM_LIQUIDITY that already prices the first share above dust?", "Does the deposit path floor-divide such that a later depositor receives exactly zero shares, and does any require(shares > 0) prevent it?", "Who is the victim, and can the attacker choose the moment a victim deposits, or does the attack need a specific victim action?", "What is the attacker cost (first deposit plus donation plus gas) versus the victim loss, and is the net positive at realistic gas prices?", "Can the attacker recover the donated amount by redeeming their own shares, or is the donation a sunk cost bounded by the theft?", "If the underlying is fee-on-transfer or rebasing, does a direct transfer bypass the bookkeeping while totalAssets still sees it?"],
      false_positives: ["totalAssets is a stored variable that donations cannot move", "OpenZeppelin ERC4626 with a non-zero decimals offset already inflating the first share", "Dead shares burned at initialization or a MINIMUM_LIQUIDITY sent to address(0)", "The vault already holds a large balance, so the required donation dwarfs the theft", "A require(shares > 0) in deposit that turns the theft into a revert", "A deposit cap or whitelist preventing the attacker from depositing", "A share price that is 1:1 by construction, such as a non-yield-bearing wrapper", "No second depositor exists in the attack window, leaving the primitive without a victim"],
      poc_must_show: ["vault totalSupply and totalAssets before the attack, plus the underlying balance", "the attacker minimum deposit and the shares received", "the donation amount and the resulting share-price multiplier", "the victim deposit and the zero or dust shares received, with exact numbers", "attacker net profit after recovering the donation and paying gas, and the victim loss", "a control run on a mitigated vault (dead shares or decimals offset) yielding no profit"],
      impact_bar: "Reportable when an unprivileged attacker causes a measurable loss to a subsequent depositor or captures unsupplied value, atomically and gas-profitable, with victim loss and attacker net profit quantified. Informational when the primitive exists but the vault is seeded, the victim set is empty, or the donation cost exceeds the theft.",
