      questions: ["Does the signed digest include block.chainid through a domain separator and the verifying contract address, or only the payload?", "Is a per-owner nonce included in the digest and incremented before any external effect?", "Can an arbitrary account submit the signature-carrying transaction, or is submission restricted to a trusted relayer?", "Does a second submission of the same signature produce a second state change or value movement?", "Is ecrecover's result checked against a zero-address return from a malformed signature?", "Does the digest use abi.encodePacked with two or more dynamic types, creating a collision surface?", "Is the nonce per-owner, per-key, or global, and can an attacker consume a global counter to invalidate a victim's pending signature?", "Is the same contract deployed at the same address on another chain with a non-empty balance while chainid is absent from the digest?"],
      false_positives: ["OpenZeppelin ERC20Permit inherited, where the domain separator and nonces are present but the grep did not follow inheritance", "An off-chain-signature design with a trusted relayer, where replay gains nothing the operator could not already do", "A nonce that is incremented in a modifier or base contract", "Signature hashes used as stored ids, where malleability is irrelevant", "chainid present in the domain separator while the reviewer inspected only a helper", "A cross-chain replay claim with no sibling deployment at the same address", "ecrecover returning zero on a path that already requires recovered == expectedSigner", "A payload containing a monotonic on-chain value that makes reuse impossible"],
      poc_must_show: ["the exact digest preimage printed from the test", "the first submission accepted with its measured effect (balance, allowance, position)", "the identical signature submitted a second time, accepted again, with the second effect measured", "a control run where the nonce is incremented or chainid added, and the second submission reverts", "for cross-chain, proof the same signature is valid at the sibling deployment and what it moves there", "for ecrecover zero, the malformed signature yielding address(0) and the authorization check still passing"],
      impact_bar: "Reportable when one signature produces two or more state changes, or a signature intended for one chain acts on another, with value or authority moving. Informational when replay has no economic effect or the path is a trusted relayer.",
