      false_positives: ["The CPI program is a hardcoded constant or a `Program<'info, Token>` typed account, so Anchor rejects a substitute before the handler runs", "The handler compares the passed program id against a stored or derived one and returns `InvalidProgramId` (3008), which is the guard working", "The accounts are derived by the program from seeds and only the instruction data is caller-supplied", "The CPI can be directed at another program but that program cannot touch the victim account, so nothing of value moves", "The instruction is admin-gated, or the CPI path is only reachable from an already-signed program-owned account"],
      poc_must_show: ["the victim account's lamport balance measured before and after on one validator, showing a decrease caused by the caller-directed CPI", "the program id the CPI was actually pointed at, printed as evidence, so a reader can see it was caller-chosen and not the expected one", "a control run passing the expected CPI program, showing the victim does not move, which attributes the loss to caller control of the target"],
      impact_bar: "Reportable when a caller-chosen CPI target causes a victim account the program holds authority over to lose lamports or tokens, quantified in lamports or token units. Informational when the CPI is redirectable but no account of value is reachable, or when the handler already pins the program and only the harness substituted it.",
