      poc_must_show: ["a keypair the program has never seen, signing a real transaction the cluster accepts, that leaves the recorded authority field equal to the attacker key", "the authority index measured before and after on the same local validator, with the fixture asserting it started at the victim's key", "the error code the correctly-guarded control run returns, so a 2002 ConstraintSigner or 3010 AccountNotSigner is named as the guard working rather than reported as a failure"],
      impact_bar: "Reportable when an account holding no role can make the program record it as authority, or can move value the recorded authority controls, with the instruction and the resulting state read back. Informational when the wrong signer can only read state, or when the check exists and the harness simply passed the wrong account.",
