      questions: ["If the implementation was left initializable, what does an attacker who initializes it gain over the upgrade path specifically: control of the implementation's own storage, a claimed slot the next upgradeTo recycles, or a layout the next version's initializer will not repair?", "Is upgradeTo or upgradeToAndCall guarded by an authority the attacker cannot obtain, and is that authority a timelock or multisig rather than an EOA?", "Do the two versions' forge inspect storageLayout outputs differ in a way that shifts an existing variable, or only append at the end?", "Was a __gap shrunk or reused, or a base contract inserted mid-inheritance, which are the shapes that silently shift layout?", "Does the initializer set every variable the implementation reads, or does an unset variable become an exploitable default such as owner == address(0)?", "Can the proxy's initialize be front-run between proxy deployment and initialization in a separate transaction?", "Are there selector clashes between the proxy's own functions and the implementation's in a non-transparent proxy?", "If the upgrade is timelocked, what is the delay, and does the program scope treat admin-only actions as in-scope?"],
      false_positives: ["A storage collision inferred by reading Solidity inheritance instead of comparing actual storage layouts", "New variables appended at the end of storage, which is safe by design", "_disableInitializers() present in the implementation constructor", "The implementation address has no code or is not deployed", "Admin-can-upgrade treated as a vulnerability when governance is a timelocked multisig and the program excludes trusted-admin risk", "A reinitializer(2) whose version was already consumed", "Mock or test proxies present in the repository", "A layout diff between versions that are not actually deployed in sequence"],
      poc_must_show: ["for the initializer bug, a fresh EOA calling initialize() on the implementation address successfully and owner() reading back as the attacker", "a control call through the proxy that reverts, proving the difference is the direct-implementation path", "for the upgrade bug, the unprivileged upgradeTo succeeding and the implementation slot changing to an attacker-controlled contract", "for a collision, both storageLayout dumps, the exact slot, the old and new variables, and a value written before the upgrade read as a different variable after it", "the value at risk through the proxy and who can withdraw it"],
      impact_bar: "Reportable when an unprivileged account can initialize or replace the implementation and thereby control funds, or a layout change demonstrably corrupts a live variable governing withdrawals, with address and amount named. Informational for shifts that touch nothing live, initializers on non-proxied contracts, or upgrade authority behind a timelock.",
