      requires: ["a low-privilege authenticated session and the ability to observe an admin or staff surface", "at least one privileged endpoint whose path, method, or payload shape can be identified", "an anonymous baseline to distinguish authentication failure from authorization failure"],
      questions: ["Which privileged endpoints exist, and is the role check enforced in the handler, in shared middleware on that route group, or only in the client that hides the menu item?", "When called with a low-privilege session, does the endpoint return 200 with privileged data, or 401 and 403 that indicate a real gate?", "Does the anonymous call fail with 401 while the low-privilege call succeeds, isolating authorization from authentication?", "Is the role or permission read from a token claim, a session record, or a request field the caller can set?", "Does a method or path variant reach the same handler without the guard, such as PATCH instead of PUT, or a trailing slash, or a different API version prefix?", "Are administrative operations exposed as separate actions on an otherwise authorized endpoint, selected by a body field rather than a distinct route?", "Does a lower role reach a superset of another role's permissions through a role hierarchy, an impersonation feature, or a support-mode header?", "Is the guard applied to the collection route but omitted on the per-item route, or the reverse?"],
